I don't think I understand that correctly. There's no "requested" capacity as in List, so ArrayPool.Rent will never throw OutOfMemory because of the hard ceiling on newCapacity. Right now MemoryMarshal.Write in Append throws an ArgumentOutOfRange, and the only way to throw OutOfMemory would be doing
```cs
if (toReturn.Length == MaxArrayLength)
{
    throw new OutOfMemoryException("Data capacity exceeded supported range.");
}
```
before any newCapacity calculations. Is that what are you asking for?
